  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "03rYZ1m8XohEXJuSEXzsan+a4PI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:21.126Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The registry holds document model modules keyed by **document type and version**, and the reactor reads it to resolve the reducer, utils and specification for a document when it executes a job. It also holds the **upgrade manifests** describing how to migrate a document up one version step.\n\nTwo details decide how lookups behave. The document type used as the key is `module.documentModel.global.id` \u2014 not a name or a package \u2014 and a module's version comes from its optional `version` field, which the registry **treats as `1` when absent**. So two different versions of the same type coexist happily, and an unversioned legacy module simply occupies slot 1.\n\n`registerModules(...modules)` returns `RegistrationResult<DocumentModelModule>[]` \u2014 one per input, **in input order** \u2014 and **never throws**. A module whose `(documentType, version)` pair is already registered produces a `DuplicateModuleError` *in its result*, and invalid or duplicate modules are skipped without affecting the rest. The default in-memory implementation is `DocumentModelRegistry`; both it and the interface are exported from `@powerhousedao/reactor`.\n\nThe practical consequence for error handling is the next note's subject: because nothing throws, a registration failure is only visible if you read the results or the logs.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/06-DocumentModelRegistry.md` \u2014 intro; IDocumentModelRegistry reference \u203a Module management \u203a registerModules\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:48:21.125Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:21.126Z"
    }
  },
